  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "Kolkata: 7 arrested over Durga Puja stampede produced before local court",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/india-news/kolkata-7-arrested-over-durga-puja-stampede-produced-before-local-court-126101800478_1.html",
      "description": "Police on Sunday produced before a local court the seven arrested persons in connection with the stampede at a Kolkata Durga Puja pandal, which resulted in the death of 19 people, a senior official said.\nTwenty-five people were also injured in the stampede at Chorbagan Durga Puja pandal in north Kolkata, following a crowd surge amid rain on Saturday evening.\n\"The arrested persons have been taken to Bankshall court. We would appeal for their custody,\" the official told PTI.\nThose arrested include the puja committee's secretary, vice-president and two employees of a private security agency.\nPolice have also registered a suo motu case of culpable homicide not amounting to murder in the case.",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-18T12:30:10"
    },
    {
      "title": "Rain, narrow exits, false alert: What led to Kolkata Puja pandal stampede?",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/india-news/kolkata-chorbagan-durga-puja-stampede-death-causes-police-probe-crowd-mismanagement-rain-126101800153_1.html",
      "description": "Police say inadequate crowd control, narrow entry and exit gates and a misleading announcement may have triggered panic at the Chorbagan pandal, leaving 19 dead and 25 injured",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-18T05:25:33"
    },
    {
      "title": "Kolkata Durga Puja stampede: Eyewitnesses flag lapses, police probe begins",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/india-news/kolkata-durga-puja-stampede-eyewitnesses-flag-lapses-police-probe-begins-126101800019_1.html",
      "description": "Kolkata Police are investigating whether lapses in crowd management, confusion over entry and exit routes and heavy rain contributed to the stampede at Chorbagan Durga Puja pandal that left 19 people dead on Saturday evening, a senior officer said.\nSeveral eyewitnesses alleged that announcements about entry, exit and crowd movement were inadequate, leaving visitors confused during the rush hours.\nLocals also claimed that police deployment at the pandal was inadequate, alleging that personnel were mainly stationed near the VIP entrance.\n\"I have not seen adequate police presence this year. This resulted in the mismanagement,\" Sanghamitra Bhowmik, a resident of the Chorbagan area, said.\nLocals also alleged that there was little administrative assistance in taking the injured to hospitals.\n\"There must be some lapses, but these should be probed. Whether lapses were on the part of the organisers or they had flouted the rules to erect the pandal will be checked,\" the police officer told",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-18T02:11:18"
    }
  ]
